(Plan 230 stage A3 — table-of-contents completeness regression guard. A
bodyless function — `To "greet".` with no body and no separating blank line —
used to absorb the following `To "c" ...` as a nested definition, so `c` was
exported by the .so but missing from the .lib: a silent .lib/.so mismatch and
the property this stage exists for. This corpus puts a bodyless function in
the middle and two bodyless in a row, each followed by another export, with NO
blank lines between them so the absorption path is exercised. test.sh builds
it as a .so and asserts the .lib ToC entry count EQUALS the nm -D
--defined-only count — a count equality, not a name list, so any future drop
fails here regardless of which function it hits.)

Library toc version "1.0".
To aa. Return a number, 1.
To greet.
To c. Return a number, 3.
To noop.
To idle.
To z. Return a number, 9.